<DocLayout slug={slug} title={title} description={description}>

Novus needs one thing: a C compiler. `gcc`, `clang` and `zig cc` all work.

## From source (recommended)

```bash
git clone https://github.com/ezTxmMC/novus
cd novus
scripts/bootstrap.sh          # or: make
```

That runs three stages and leaves `build/novusc`:

| Stage | What happens |
|---|---|
| 0 | `cc bootstrap/novusc.c -o build/novusc0` - the checked-in snapshot |
| 1 | the snapshot compiles the current `compiler/*.nv` sources |
| 2 | the result compiles itself again - that binary is `build/novusc` |

```bash
build/novusc version
# novusc 0.1.0-pre.alpha.8
```

### Windows

With `gcc` from MinGW-w64 / MSYS2 on the `PATH`:

```bash
scripts\bootstrap.cmd
# or
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\bootstrap.ps1
```

`set NOVUS_CC=clang` picks a different compiler.

## Download a release

Tagged releases on [GitHub](https://github.com/ezTxmMC/novus/releases) carry a
binary of the compiler and of the language server for every target. Releases
whose tag has a suffix (`v0.1.0-pre.alpha.8`) are marked as pre-releases.

| Target | Files |
|---|---|
| Linux x86-64 (glibc 2.17+) | `novusc-x86_64-linux-gnu`, `novus-lsp-x86_64-linux-gnu` |
| Linux x86-64 (musl, static) | `novusc-x86_64-linux-musl`, `novus-lsp-x86_64-linux-musl` |
| Linux ARM64 | `novusc-aarch64-linux-gnu`, `novus-lsp-aarch64-linux-gnu` |
| macOS Intel / Apple silicon | `novusc-x86_64-macos`, `novusc-aarch64-macos` (and `novus-lsp-...`) |
| Windows x86-64 / ARM64 | `novusc-x86_64-windows-gnu.exe`, `novusc-aarch64-windows-gnu.exe` (and `novus-lsp-...`) |

### Linux

Download the file for your machine (`uname -m` prints `x86_64` or `aarch64`),
make it executable and move it into a directory on the `PATH` under the name
`novusc`. `/usr/bin` needs root:

```bash
TARGET=x86_64-linux-gnu                         # or aarch64-linux-gnu, x86_64-linux-musl
BASE=https://github.com/ezTxmMC/novus/releases/latest/download

curl -fLO $BASE/novusc-$TARGET
curl -fLO $BASE/novus-lsp-$TARGET               # the language server, optional

chmod +x novusc-$TARGET novus-lsp-$TARGET
sudo mv novusc-$TARGET /usr/bin/novusc
sudo mv novus-lsp-$TARGET /usr/bin/novus-lsp

novusc version
```

`releases/latest/download/<file>` always points at the newest release; replace
`latest/download` by `download/<tag>` (for example `download/v0.1.0-pre.alpha.8`)
to pin a version. GitHub does not count pre-releases as "latest": while only
pre-releases exist, the `latest` URL answers 404 and the tag has to be named.

`/usr/local/bin` works the same way and keeps the files apart from the ones of
the package manager. Without root, use `~/.local/bin` (no `sudo`) and make sure
it is on the `PATH`. `novusc` compiles to C, so a C compiler (`gcc`, `clang`
or `zig cc`) still has to be installed.

### macOS

The system folders are protected, so use `/usr/local/bin`:

```bash
curl -fLO https://github.com/ezTxmMC/novus/releases/latest/download/novusc-aarch64-macos
chmod +x novusc-aarch64-macos
sudo mv novusc-aarch64-macos /usr/local/bin/novusc
xattr -d com.apple.quarantine /usr/local/bin/novusc
```

### Windows

Download `novusc-x86_64-windows-gnu.exe`, rename it to `novusc.exe` and put it
into a folder that is on the `PATH`. `gcc` from MinGW-w64 / MSYS2 has to be on
the `PATH` as well.

<Callout type="note">
Every push to the repository also builds these binaries: the `artifacts` of the
CI run on GitHub hold the same files for the latest commit.
</Callout>

### Build the binaries yourself

Seven targets are cross compiled from a single machine with
[zig](https://ziglang.org):

```bash
scripts/cross.sh              # -> dist/
scripts/cross.sh aarch64-macos  # just one target
```

<Callout type="warning">
macOS binaries built through zig are not code signed. Run
`xattr -d com.apple.quarantine novusc-aarch64-macos` once after downloading.
</Callout>

## Environment variables

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `NOVUS_CC` | C compiler used to build programs (default `cc`, `gcc` on Windows) |
| `NOVUS_CFLAGS` | extra flags handed to the C compiler |
| `NOVUS_ZIG` | zig executable used for `--target` cross builds |
| `NOVUS_DEPS` | module cache for dependencies (default `~/.novus/deps`) |

## Verifying the installation

```bash
make test
```

runs the golden tests, all 258 examples and the self-hosting ladder including
the fixpoint check.

## Editor support

The VS Code extension in `vscode-novus/` provides highlighting, a language
server with diagnostics and navigation, and run/build commands - see
[Editor support](/docs/projects/editor).

